# Copy to web/.env.local and fill both values.
#
# Both of these are PUBLIC. Anything prefixed with VITE_ is inlined into the
# JavaScript bundle at build time and is readable by anyone who loads the page.
# That is fine for these two: the project URL is public, and the anon key is a
# project identifier that grants no access on its own - row access is decided
# by Supabase RLS after a user signs in.
#
# NEVER put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here, or any other server-only secret.
# It bypasses RLS entirely and lives only in GitHub Actions secrets.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Refresh button additionally needs three SERVER-side variables, used only
# by the functions in web/api/. They have no VITE_ prefix, so Vite cannot
# inline them and the browser can never read them.
#
#   GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN   fine-grained PAT, Stacheydev/NBLG only,
#                           Actions: Read and write
#   SUPABASE_URL            same value as VITE_SUPABASE_URL above
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY       same value as VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY above
#
# Set them in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings -> Environment
# Variables). Do NOT add them to this file or to .env.local: those exist for
# the browser build, and GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN is a real credential.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
